  {
   "id": "c54b134d-7726-485f-8ad8-eb35d1cef020",
   "type": "author",
   "attributes": {
    "biography": {
     "en": "Toyonaka Ozaki (尾崎 豊中), also known as Toyo Ozaki, was an art designer who worked at SEGA in the late 80's to early '90s. She is best known for designing the characters in Phantasy Star III: Generations of Doom. She is named after Toyonaka, a city in the Osaka Prefecture prefecture, which she is a native of. She is a fan of manga artist Hiroshi Motomiya."
    },
